name chess-com
# Games played on chess.com, as its public archive gives them: one PGN file a player's archive (a fetch of the chess
# lab, FabianoCaruana_chesscom.pgn: 4,673 games). PGN is the PGN standard's export format; chess.com writes its own
# tags beside the Seven Tag Roster (Link, Timezone, StartTime, EndDate, EndTime, CurrentPosition, ECO, ECOUrl,
# Tournament, Variant, SetUp, FEN) and a clock comment ([%clk]) after every move. A PGN is one corpus witnessing its
# records, as ToxiGen is: White and Black are participants named in each record, content as written, never witnesses
# (Sequence 9, Sources).
witness Chess.com
# StructuredCorpus: the class Sequence 9 (the estate) gives the game collections
class StructuredCorpus
root $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/Initial-Corpus/*.pgn
files $LAPLACE_DATA/Games/Chess/later-corpus/*.pgn
after unicode
